        "summary": "χMT = 56.41 cm3 K mol−1 at 300 K decreases to 40.10 cm3 K mol−1 at 2.0 K. Zero-dc-field ac susceptibility (2–20 K, 1–10000 Hz) shows temperature- and frequency-dependent in-phase and out-of-phase signals with two peaks, indicating SMM behavior and two relaxation processes. Arrhenius fit of τ from χ″ peaks gives ΔE/kB = 52.65 K and τ0 = 7.01×10−7 s. Cole–Cole plots (2.0–16.0 K) fit a generalized Debye model with α = 0.24–0.54.",
